---
description: GitLab is the working copy; GitHub is a public mirror of main only
alwaysApply: true
---

GitLab (`origin`) is the working copy. GitHub is a public mirror of `main` only.

Do not commit `.cursor/` (except `.cursor/rules/`), `.venv/`, `data/credentials.json`, `data/worklog.db`, `data/*.xlsx`, `data/backups/`, or `worklog-windows-*.zip`.

Do not push topic branches to GitHub. Do not add a GitHub remote. Do not "sync all branches". After a Cursor or feature branch is merged to `main` on GitLab, delete the source branch.

Do not force-push `main`.
